**Problema:**
- Dropout desativa 20% dos neurônios
- Mas **NÃO escala** os 80% ativos
- Isso causa **expectation shift**

**Teoria (Srivastava et al., 2014):**
```
Durante treino: y = dropout(x) · W
Durante teste: y = x · (W · p)  // Onde p = keep_prob

OU

Durante treino: y = dropout(x) · W / p  // Inverted dropout
Durante teste: y = x · W
Correção:


cpp
PredictionResult PredictMC(double &f[]) {
   double samples[30];
   double dropout_rate = 0.2;
   double keep_prob = 1.0 - dropout_rate;
   
   for(int k=0; k<30; k++) {
      MathSrand((int)(GetMicrosecondCount() + k*1000)); // ✅ Re-seed
      
      double z = bias;
      int active_count = 0;
      
      for(int i=0; i<MAX_FEATURES; i++) {
         if (MathRand() % 1000 >= (int)(dropout_rate * 1000)) {
            z += weights[i] * f[i];
            active_count++;
         }
      }
      
      // ✅ Escala para compensar dropout (Inverted Dropout)
      if(active_count > 0) {
         z *= (double)MAX_FEATURES / active_count;
      }
      
      samples[k] = 1.0 / (1.0 + MathExp(-z));
   }
   
   // Calcular estatísticas
   PredictionResult res;
   double sum = 0, sum_sq = 0;
   for(int i=0; i<30; i++) {
      sum += samples[i];
      sum_sq += samples[i] * samples[i];
   }
   res.probability = sum / 30;
   res.uncertainty = MathSqrt(sum_sq/30 - res.probability*res.probability);
   
   return res;
}

